{"type": "message", "id": "39841999", "parentId": "2165c41e", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T06:24:42.415Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I now have the detailed financial data from Tesla's 10-K filing. Let me extract the key numbers:\n\nFrom the Financial Summary table, I can see:\n\n**Revenues:**\n- Q1 2023: $23,329 million\n- Q2 2023: $24,927 million\n- Q3 2023: $23,350 million\n- Q4 2023: $25,167 million\n\n**Net Income (GAAP):**\n- Q1 2023: $2,539 million\n- Q2 2023: $2,614 million\n- Q3 2023: $1,878 million\n- Q4 2023: $7,943 million (note: this includes a one-time non-cash tax benefit of $5.9B)\n\nNow let me calculate the net profit margin for each quarter using the formula: (Net Income / Total Revenues) × 100\n\n**Q1 2023:** (2,539 / 23,329) × 100 = 10.88%\n**Q2 2023:** (2,614 / 24,927) × 100 = 10.49%\n**Q3 2023:** (1,878 / 23,350) × 100 = 8.04%\n**Q4 2023:** (7,943 / 25,167) × 100 = 31.56%\n\nWait, I need to verify these numbers are correct. Let me search for more specific data to confirm, particularly the Q4 numbers since they include a one-time tax benefit."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "functions.web_search:15", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "Tesla Q1 2023 net income revenue millions 10-Q first quarter", "count": 5}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "modelstudio", "model": "kimi-k2.5", "usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 0, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775283864049, "responseId": "chatcmpl-b14bcf56-b259-9090-af7c-29ec3254814a"}}
